# Binaries.
#
# These patterns are anchored to the repository root with a leading slash. An
# unanchored "tlsanalyzer" also matches the cmd/tlsanalyzer DIRECTORY, which
# silently excluded every file in it: cmd/tlsanalyzer/port_test.go, the
# regression tests for the 0.3.0 --port and --format fixes, was never committed
# and never ran in CI, while the local suite passed because Go does not consult
# git. See the "test files are tracked" step in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
/tlsanalyzer
/tlsanalyzer.exe
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Credentials.
#
# Unlike the binary patterns above these are deliberately NOT anchored: they are
# filenames rather than build outputs, and a stray copy anywhere in the tree must
# be ignored. Template files are excluded from the exclusion, because they hold
# placeholders and are meant to be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
!testdata/**/*.key
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Test outputs
*.out
coverage.html
coverage.txt

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
